jobs.description:
- Venlo - 40 uur - € 15,68 per uur 
Are you someone who likes to roll up their sleeves, works accurately and enjoys a dynamic working environment? Then we are looking for you! As a Warehouse Employee, you will work in a modern distribution centre in Venlo, where you and your colleagues are responsible for processing and preparing orders for shipment across Europe and the Middle East. 
What do we offer? 
• A gross hourly wage of €15.68; 
• A full-time position of 40 hours per week; 
• A high chance of receiving a permanent contract; 
• Double pay on Sundays and public holidays; 
• Travel allowance of €0.21 per kilometre; 
• Flexible day shifts between 07:00 and 19:00; 
• 30% overtime allowance; 
• 200% pay on Sundays; 
• Paid training and plenty of opportunities for personal and professional development; 
• Working in a modern and sustainable distribution centre in Venlo; 
• An international and dynamic working environment; 
• Access to an exclusive Sample Sale featuring well-known fashion brands. 
What will you do? 
As a Warehouse Employee, you are an important part of the logistics process. 
Your responsibilities will include: - Picking and processing orders for customers across Europe and the Middle East; - Picking fashion items in the warehouse; - Moving and processing goods within the warehouse; - Checking orders and preparing them for shipment; - Identifying and reporting discrepancies and quality issues; - Working together with colleagues and supervisors to ensure orders are processed correctly and on time; - Keeping the workplace clean and safe; - Working according to applicable safety and quality regulations. 
What do you bring? - You are willing to work weekends; - You speak and understand English, as this is the main language spoken on the work floor; - You are motivated, reliable and hardworking; - You work accurately and have an eye for quality; - Experience in logistics is a plus, but motivation and a good work ethic are...

We do have a few wishes before we can offer you this job:
-- You will need to have a C driving license with code 95;
-- You speak and understand Dutch or English well;  
-- You are customer-friendly, flexible and solution-oriented;     
-- You handle fresh food products with care.           

NICE VACANCY FOR A TRUCK DRIVER 

-- EARN MONEY WHILE DRIVING THROUGH THE NETHERLANDS?
-- Yes, that will be possible soon!

-- At a renowned fresh food and catering company, you can pick up the most tasteful culinary dishes and deliver them to various hotels, restaurants, healthcare institutions or simply to festivals and private parties!

-- You travel a lot and therefore work many hours, for which you get paid!
& every day fresh and healthy snacks are ready for you on the go! 

-- We offer you:
-- A good working atmosphere with motivated and experienced colleagues;
-- A comfortable truck;
-- Excellent primary and secondary employment conditions, in accordance with the collective labor agreement;
-- Development opportunities and training.
-------- If you are interested, please let us know!

In line with our expectations, we expect our team members to be passionate about their work, to act with honesty and integrity, and to have a healthy dose of enthusiasm. The desired skills for the Quality Control Employee are also:
*  At least MBO level of working and thinking;
* 2-3 years work experience as a Quality Control Employee in a food company;
* Flexibility: working in four overlapping shifts, with Saturdays occasionally forming part of the working week;
* Fluency in spoken and written English; Dutch is an advantage;
* Knowledge of HACCP and GFSI;
* Strong communication skills, persuasive and decisive;
* Works accurately and is proactive;
* You are proficient in Excel and Word.

The New Plant - At The New Plant we produce Beyond Meats plant-based protein products for customers in Europe, the middle East and parts of Africa. Beyond Meat has been partnering with McDonalds sinds 2021 and supplies the vegetarian patty for the McPlant. Within your team, you will be working alongside three Quality Control Employee, a Quality Control Supervisor and a Quality Control Manager, and you will collaborate with two Quality Assurance Assistants.

A leading Spanish organization in the comprehensive logistics sector with over 14,000 people in 21 countries is recruiting talent for their warehouse in Amsterdam.

What are you going to do?
•    Loading/unloading and build of air freight plates;
•    Sorting and scanning the freight;
•    Structure of shipments following the contours manuals and manifest;
•    Processing the air cargo;
•    Forklift activities
•    Keep the workplace nice and tidy;
•    Support the Team Leader in carrying out warehouse activities.

Who are we looking for?
•    Experience with air freight;
•    You are prepared to work in 3 shifts
•    VGB and Air Freight certificate;
•    You are able to speak English;
•    You are willing to work during the weekends.

What do we offer?
•    A competitive salary;
•    Possibility of a permanent contract in long-term;
•    Irregularity shift allowances of at least 35% up to 145% on top of your current hourly salary;
•    Overtime paid (30%) after 40 hours a week;
•    Pension premium free, (paid by employer);
•    8% holiday allowance;
•    Travel allowance of € 0.23 per kilometer;
•    26 paid vacation days per year;
•    An exciting, challenging, and independent job in a dynamic company with a direct and open communication culture and an informal atmosphere.
